"program_narrative": "Program CURSMGR is an online (CICS) program that receives a cursor request in CURSOR-REQUEST-AREA (PROCEDURE DIVISION USING) and dispatches on the request type: 'D' declares a cursor, 'O' opens it, 'F' and 'C' perform fetch and close paragraphs that are not present in the source file. It reads no files; it issues embedded SQL DECLARE CURSOR and OPEN statements whose cursor name and statement text come from the caller's host variables CURS-NAME and CURS-STMT. Declaring sets the working array size to WS-MAX-ROWS when array fetch is requested, otherwise to 1; opening resets the fetch and row counters. After each SQL statement the SQLCODE is copied into CURS-RESPONSE-CODE when it is non-zero (and 0 is set when OPEN succeeds). A request type other than D/O/F/C performs nothing. Every path ends with EXEC CICS RETURN to the caller. The source file is truncated at line 91, so the fetch and close logic cannot be traced.",
